@startuml
actor User
participant Main
participant DemoSeed
participant ConsoleApplication
participant ConsoleInput
participant BookingFacade
participant AppointmentAssembler
participant InMemoryAppointmentRepository
participant CommittedEventDispatcher
participant AppointmentEventPublisher
participant ExternalCalendarAdapter
Main -> DemoSeed : create(runtime Clock, zone)
Main -> BookingFacade : wire one repository/dispatcher/creators
Main -> DemoSeed : populate(facade)
DemoSeed -> BookingFacade : book + confirm previous weekday
DemoSeed -> DemoSeed : permanently delegate clock to runtime
Main -> ConsoleApplication : run()
User -> ConsoleInput : selections, date/time, options
ConsoleApplication -> BookingFacade : available(request) [advisory]
BookingFacade -> AppointmentAssembler : assemble via Builder/creators
ConsoleApplication -> User : review quote, mode and resolved offset
User -> ConsoleInput : confirm y
ConsoleApplication -> BookingFacade : book(command UUID, request)
BookingFacade -> CommittedEventDispatcher : execute
CommittedEventDispatcher -> InMemoryAppointmentRepository : atomic reserve / event append
InMemoryAppointmentRepository -> InMemoryAppointmentRepository : hard rules + Strategy
CommittedEventDispatcher -> AppointmentEventPublisher : publish after store unlock
AppointmentEventPublisher -> AppointmentEventPublisher : notification + audit observers
CommittedEventDispatcher -> ExternalCalendarAdapter : synchronize simulated mirror
BookingFacade --> ConsoleApplication : BookingResult + delivery warnings
ConsoleApplication -> User : ID, shortcut, fees, PENDING
note over ConsoleApplication, BookingFacade
Confirm, reschedule, cancel and complete use the same facade.
State and repository enforce all lifecycle/scheduling rules.
EOF unwinds pending input without writing.
end note
@enduml
